# GrowCold Shared Package Guide

`packages/shared` contains code used by both `apps/web` and `apps/mobile`. When a piece of logic, schema, or utility is needed in more than one app, put it here.

## What belongs in packages/shared

- `packages/shared/src/api/**` — API client, endpoint definitions, typed response parsing
- `packages/shared/src/components/**` — UI components safe for both React Native and web
- `packages/shared/src/hooks/**` — shared hooks (e.g., `useOnlineStatus`, `useOfflineQueue`)
- `packages/shared/src/store/**` — Zustand stores (offline queue, warehouse context)
- `packages/shared/src/schemas/**` — Zod schemas and API contracts
- `packages/shared/src/utils/**` — pure utilities (formatINR, formatDate, etc.)
- `packages/shared/src/i18n/**` / `packages/shared/src/locales/**` — translation files
- `packages/shared/src/offline/**` — offline queue and sync abstractions

## Technical rules for shared code

- TypeScript strict mode and Zod at all external boundaries
- **Platform-agnostic only** — no DOM-only APIs (`window`, `document`, browser globals) — this code runs on React Native too
- Use `@supabase/supabase-js` for Supabase access. Accept runtime config (`supabaseUrl`, `supabaseAnonKey`) from the app layer — do not read env vars directly in shared
- Keep utilities pure and side-effect free
- Keep hooks compliant with React hook rules
- Export public APIs through barrel exports (`packages/shared/src/index.ts` and sub-index files)

## API contracts

Define typed contracts under `packages/shared/src/api/endpoints/[resource].ts` before implementing consumers. Example:

```typescript
// packages/shared/src/api/endpoints/lots.ts
export const GetLotsRequest = z.object({
  warehouseId: z.string(),
  status: z.enum(['ACTIVE', 'STALE']).optional(),
});
export type GetLotsRequest = z.infer<typeof GetLotsRequest>;
```

## Commit format

- `feat: add offline queue abstraction`
- `fix: handle sync conflict in lot schema`
